      "heading": "Iteration: feed it back in",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "To iterate means to repeat a rule, feeding each output back in.",
          "write": "output → next input"
        },
        {
          "say": "A recurrence rule tells you how to get the next term from this one.",
          "write": "uₙ₊₁ = 1.1uₙ − 50"
        },
        {
          "say": "You also need a starting value, u nought.",
          "write": "u₀ = 1000"
        },
        {
