    {
      "heading": "Steady state",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Some rules settle at a steady value, called a steady state.",
          "write": "uₙ₊₁ = 0.5uₙ + 40"
        },
        {
          "say": "Replace both terms with L and solve.",
          "write": "L = 0.5L + 40"
        },
        {
          "say": "Half of L is 40, so L is 80.",
          "write": "L = 80"
        },
        {
          "say": "This works when a is between 0 and 1.",
          "write": "L = b ÷ (1 − a)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The Babylonian method",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "To find root N, start with a guess and repeat this rule.",
          "write": "new x = (x + N ÷ x) ÷ 2"
        },
        {
          "say": "Find root 10. Start with x equals 2. That's a 2 by 5 rectangle.",
          "write": "x₀ = 2",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Rectangle of area 10 getting more square",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 230,
                "y": 25,
                "w": 100,
                "h": 250,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "2 × 5"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 290,
                "text": "area = 10",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "grey",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Average 2 and 5. The new x is 3.5.",
          "write": "x₁ = (2 + 5) ÷ 2 = 3.5",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Rectangle of area 10 getting more square",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 193,
                "y": 79,
                "w": 175,
                "h": 142,
                "fill": "orange",
                "change": "add",
                "label": "3.5 × 2.857"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 290,
                "text": "area = 10",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "grey",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Again. The new x is about 3.1786. Nearly square.",
          "write": "x₂ ≈ 3.1786",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Rectangle of area 10 getting more square",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 201,
                "y": 72,
                "w": 158,
                "h": 157,
                "fill": "orange",
                "change": "add",
                "label": "3.179 × 3.146"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 290,
                "text": "area = 10",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "grey",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Each step makes the rectangle more square. Its side heads to root 10.",
          "write": "√10 ≈ 3.1623"
        },
        {
          "say": "If x is too small, N over x is too big. Their average is closer."
        }
      ]
